# Project Structure Template

Purpose:
  This directory contains reusable schemas, indexes, and routing tables
  for the project model. Concrete project data is NOT stored here.

Contents:
  This directory is SCHEMA-ONLY. For reusable templates, see:
    @../../templates/INDEX.sdd

  Model files:
    project.sdd     — Project model entry point (shape, schema, rules)
    domains.sdd     — Domain schema and list
    modules.sdd     — Module schema and list
    map.sdd         — Project navigation map
    flows.sdd       — Execution flow schema
    dependencies.sdd — Dependency schema
    indexes.sdd     — Category-level index schema
    instantiation.sdd — Project instantiation rules
    mode.sdd        — Project mode schema
    architecture.sdd — Architecture schema
    README.sdd      — This file

Usage:
  1. This folder defines HOW projects are structured (the model)
  2. Concrete project instances live in .sdd/projects/<name>/
  3. Templates for decisions, tasks, docs, etc. live in templates/_sdd/
  4. When a new project is initiated, it is instantiated from this model

Note:
  This directory does NOT contain concrete project data.
  Concrete project data lives in:
    - .sdd/projects/<name>/decisions/ (concrete decisions)
    - .sdd/projects/<name>/tasks/ (concrete tasks)
    - .sdd/projects/<name>/docs/ (concrete docs)
    - .sdd/projects/<name>/stack/ (concrete stack)
    - .sdd/projects/<name>/ (all other project state)

State: +
